{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\nPure mutation plans still need to represent binding lifecycle decisions and prerequisite ordering without performing effects. Selection, filters, mode caps, and safety limits must exclude work before intents are eligible.\n\n## Outcome\nAdd versioned lifecycle intents and explicit inter-ticket dependencies to `TicketPlan`, and apply every global selection/limit before any lifecycle or remote effect.\n\n## Plan\n1. Model bind, confirm, re-key, retire, baseline, and comment-identity changes as versioned intents only. Each intent's `version` is the enclosing frozen `Observation.version` identity from S2 T1 (its `ObservationVersion` — the content-hash `fingerprint` plus `pass_id`); intents carry no independent counter, so pure oracle tables assert `intent.version == observation.version` exactly.\n2. Encode create-before-link and parent-before-child prerequisites. A blocked prerequisite yields a deferred disposition carrying reason `dependency_deferred` and emits no out-of-order mutation.\n3. Move selection, filter, mode cap, and global safety limit decisions into pre-effect planning, each recording a distinguishable deferral reason (see \"Dispositions\" below).\n4. Cover tombstones, pending/index lag, moved keys, impossible links, partial snapshots, and filtered passes with ticket-sourced tables, each mapping to a deterministic disposition + reason.\n\n## Dispositions (deferral reason vocabulary)\n`PlanDisposition` keeps `mutate`/`defer`/`noop`; a deferred/excluded plan additionally records a `defer_reason` drawn from the existing apply-layer `operation_outcome.Disposition` names, so each AC outcome family is separately assertable:\n- blocked prerequisite (create-before-link / parent-before-child) -> `dependency_deferred`\n- selection / filter exclusion -> `scope_deferred`\n- mode cap / global safety limit exclusion -> `safety_aborted`\n- tombstone / index-lag / moved-key / impossible-link / partial-snapshot -> `skipped`\n\n## Impacted sites (existing construction/consumer surface)\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/ticket_plan.py` — `TicketPlan` value type: gains versioned lifecycle-intent and inter-ticket-dependency fields plus the `defer_reason` field (kept frozen, provider-neutral, open payload).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/ticket_planner.py` — `plan_pass` (currently groups mutations by target only, ticket_planner.py:110-126): gains intent/dependency derivation and pre-effect selection/filter/mode-cap/limit exclusion with reason tagging. Stays pure (zero I/O).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/run_differs.py:285` — the shadow construction site `ctx.observation, ctx.ticket_plans = ticket_planner.plan_pass(... selection=..., limits=..., mode=...)`. **In scope:** it adopts the new pre-effect selection/filter/mode-cap/limit behavior and the widened `TicketPlan` surface by calling the updated `plan_pass`; it already forwards `selection`/`limits`/`mode`, so any `plan_pass` signature change is reflected at this call site. It remains a pure, additive shadow attach performing no effects.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_ticket_plan_shadow.py` — held-out oracle extended for intents/dependencies/pre-effect exclusion.\n\n## Testing\nPure tables assert exact intent values (including `version == observation.version`), dependency edges, and per-family `(disposition, defer_reason)` pairs, and poison repository/provider writes. Ordering tests vary each limit independently.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every named binding change is represented as a lifecycle intent whose `version` equals the enclosing `Observation.version` identity.\n- [ ] No lifecycle intent performs any write during planning (all repository/provider write seams poisoned).\n- [ ] Create-before-link prerequisites are explicit plan dependencies.\n- [ ] Parent-before-child prerequisites are explicit plan dependencies.\n- [ ] Blocked prerequisites produce deferred plans tagged `dependency_deferred`.\n- [ ] Blocked prerequisites emit no out-of-order mutation.\n- [ ] Selection and filter exclusion produce plans tagged `scope_deferred` before any intent or remote effect is eligible.\n- [ ] Mode cap and global safety limit exclusion produce plans tagged `safety_aborted` before any intent or remote effect is eligible.\n- [ ] Ticket-sourced tombstone, index-lag, move, impossible-link, and partial-snapshot cases produce deterministic `skipped` dispositions.\n\n## Out of scope\nPreview output rendering and production coordinator execution. The `run_differs.py:285` shadow construction site is in scope only for adopting the updated `plan_pass` signature/semantics (above); it does not gain preview rendering or effectful execution."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787605379230774001,"uuid":"c3874280-24b0-4956-b99f-aff44c5f8015"}